{"chunk_id": "9f0af1eac2f2", "text": "After a day of brutal carnage, both armies withdraw at sunset, their warriors blood\u2011soaked and exhausted. In the Kaurava camp, Duryodhana angrily rebukes Drona for failing to capture Yudhishthira despite his vow. Ashamed but resolute, Drona explains that as long as Arjuna and Krishna guard the Pandavas, victory is nearly impossible. He promises instead to slay a great Pandava hero and prepares an impenetrable battle formation, provided Arjuna is lured away. The Samsaptakas draw Arjuna to another front, allowing Drona\u2019s plan to unfold. Abhimanyu, Arjuna\u2019s young son, bravely penetrates the formidable circular array and devastates the Kaurava forces before being surrounded and killed by multiple warriors. His death brings jubilation to the Kauravas but grief and moral unease, prompting Dhritarashtra to question the righteousness of slaying such a youth.\nDrona forms an impenetrable array after luring Arjuna away; Abhimanyu breaks in, fights heroically, and is slain by multiple Kaurava warriors.\nThemes: Abhimanyu's death, battle strategy, duty of Kshatriyas, deception in war, grief and moral conflict", "vector": [-0.012841165997087955, -0.005112302955240011, -0.008581489324569702, 0.023252176120877266, -0.012364800088107586, 0.03584480285644531, -0.01596170850098133, -0.010645740665495396, -0.022175176069140434, -0.020642520859837532, 0.022920791059732437, 0.018212363123893738, 0.005550697911530733, 0.01050766371190548, 0.0003275015333201736, 0.009582547470927238, 0.039849039167165756, -0.009768951684236526, 0.02442583069205284, -0.024066831916570663, -0.010286740958690643, -0.008760989643633366, 0.0004267444019205868, 0.027063103392720222, -0.01033506728708744, 0.02913425862789154, -0.010417914018034935, -0.02929995208978653, 0.008360565640032291, -0.01150872278958559, -0.005333226174116135, -0.004791273735463619, 0.00030657422030344605, -0.002689050743356347, -0.02018686570227146, 0.00923045165836811, -0.0137248598